        <briefdescription>
<para>Version generique de I2C1_BusRecovery() pour n&apos;importe quel bus : passe SCL/SDA en sorties open-drain, envoie jusqu&apos;a 9 fronts d&apos;horloge pour qu&apos;un esclave bloque relache SDA, genere un STOP manuel, puis remet les broches en fonction alternative I2C. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>port</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Port GPIO des deux broches (ex : GPIOB). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>scl_pin</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Broche SCL (ex : GPIO_PIN_10 pour I2C2). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>sda_pin</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Broche SDA (ex : GPIO_PIN_11 pour I2C2). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>af_i2c</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Fonction alternative I2C a restaurer (ex : GPIO_AF4_I2C2). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="retval"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Aucun</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>(void). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Exemple d&apos;utilisation</title><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>Bus<sp/>I2C2<sp/>bloque<sp/>(SDA<sp/>tenue<sp/>a<sp/>0<sp/>par<sp/>un<sp/>esclave)<sp/>:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">I2C_BusRecovery(GPIOB,<sp/>GPIO_PIN_10,<sp/>GPIO_PIN_11,<sp/>GPIO_AF4_I2C2);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">MX_I2C2_Init();</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
